{"page_content": "5.1\nExperiment Requirements\nFLEX-2\nSRD Rev. 1\n5.1.4\nInitial Ambient\nThe ambient oxygen mole fraction in\ufb02uences the burning rate, extinction diameter, \ufb02ame chem-\nistry and \ufb02ame characteristics (size, temperature). This parameter will vary from 0.4 down\nto the limit where no \ufb02ame can be sustained at any droplet diameter. The diluents used in\nthe present study will be nitrogen and helium. Note that both nitrogen and helium are bio-\ncompatible and helium help control the \ufb02ame temperature.\nOxygen mole fraction:\nThe oxygen mole fraction shall range from 0.1 \u22120.4 \u00b1 0.005.\nDiluent type:\nDiluents shall consist of either N2 or He.\nDiluent mole fraction:\nThe diluent mole fractions shall vary depending upon the oxygen\nconcentration speci\ufb01ed for each test.\nAmbient quiescence:\nGases shall be well-mixed and quiescent prior to ignition.\nAmbient temperature:\nThe initial chamber gas temperature shall be within 18 oC\u221227 oC.\nRelative humidity:\nThe chamber relative humidity shall be less than 10% for all the test\npoints.\n5.1.5\nDroplet Translation\nOne objective of FLEX-2 is to study slow convective \ufb02ow e\ufb00ects on burning characteristics. The\n\u201c\ufb02ow \ufb01eld\u201d may be established around the droplet by translating a tethered droplet to induce\nan e\ufb00ective \ufb02ow \ufb01eld. This method would provide precise control over the imposed \ufb02ow and\nwould allow accurate control of the \ufb02ow acceleration/deceleration, particularly at low speeds.\nDuring combustion the droplet continually shrinks in size and the Reynolds number, based\non instantaneous droplet diameter, continually decreases if the \ufb02ow velocity is not increased\nwith time. In order to maintain a desired Reynolds number during combustion and to study\n\ufb02ow induced transient e\ufb00ects it is requested that the translation velocity is controllable with\nprescribed acceleration/deceleration values that are selectable for speci\ufb01c test runs.\nDroplet translation velocity:\nThe tethered droplet translation velocity shall be selectable\nfor a given test between 0.1 cm/sec to 5 cm/sec \u00b1 1%.\nDroplet acceleration/deceleration:\nThe tethered droplet translation acceleration/deceleration\nshall be selectable for a given test.\n36", "metadata": {"source": "FLEX-2 SRD Final.pdf", "page": 42}}